From: =?UTF-8?q?Bedirhan=20Gen=C3=A7aslan?=
 <b2210356065@cs.hacettepe.edu.tr>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 17:43:41 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 64/71] Keep a verbatim tail of assistant answers through
 compaction

Upstream compaction keeps the user's own messages and one summary; every answer
the model wrote is destroyed. Measured on the one compaction recorded since
`1315edcd16`, that leaves the model 618 tokens of its own output against the
73,314 it was shown, written by the cheap model, and it re-reads files it had
just read.

The tail comes back as it was: `select_retained_assistant_tail` walks request
groups newest-first and keeps those that fit whole, so the boundary is a pure
function of the history and stays stable across turns, which is what lets the
prompt prefix keep hitting cache. Commentary-phase chatter and tool traffic are
skipped. `retained_assistant_tail_note` tells the summarizer which requests are
preserved so it does not spend output describing them again.

The budget is 6_000, not the 10_000 it carried before. Until `89fef09581` the
text was assembled through `content_items_to_text` over one `OutputText` part
per streamed token, so a newline landed between every token: measured over the
332 messages retained by the recorded compactions, 45,101 tokens stored against
21,773 for the same text concatenated. The old 10_000 therefore bought about
6,960 tokens of real content and billed about 14,400. 6_000 buys the same
content for half the tokens, and puts the post-compaction floor near 10k instead
of 17k, leaving more runway to the 80k limit.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
